course: dictionary
lesson: 11709
title: Augment: adding to make it better
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Augment is a formal word. It means to make something bigger, stronger or better by adding to it. Look for the clue of adding more. «The school will augment its library with forty new books.» The school adds forty books, so the library grows.
explain: Augment is a verb, so it changes its form: augments, augmented and augmenting. «The coach augmented the team with two strong players.» Ask yourself: is something being added to make it better? If yes, augment fits. Try your meaning in the sentence: "added to the team with two strong players" still makes sense.
explain: Adults use augment in formal writing and speech. «She hopes to augment her income with a weekend job.» Her income is the money she earns, and a weekend job adds more money. In maths and music, augment also means making something larger.
fact: Augment means to make something bigger, stronger or better by adding to it.
fact: Augment is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in serious writing and speech.
fact: Augment is a verb: augment, augments, augmented, augmenting.
fact: In music, to augment an interval means to make it larger.
fact: Augmented reality adds pictures to the real world on a screen.
exercise: «The school will augment its library with forty new books.» What does augment mean here? | To close something down | To take something away | To paint something a new colour | *To make something bigger by adding to it
exercise: «The team wants to augment its strength with a new coach.» Which meaning fits? | To lose something on purpose | To count something quietly | *To make something stronger by adding to it | To rest after a game
exercise: Fill the gap: «Yesterday she ___ her income with a second job.» | augmenting | augment | augments | *augmented
test: «The chef added spices to augment the flavour of the soup.» What does augment mean? | To cool something down | To hide something from view | *To make something better by adding to it | To remove something from it
test: Which phrase describes adding pictures to the real world on a screen? | Fast reading | Silent screen | *Augmented reality | Hidden reality
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to augment? | Hide | *Increase | Forget | Shrink
